{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:27-2","provision":"BCO 27-2","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"27-2","title":"Section 27-2","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/27-2/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/27-2","current_text":{"html":"<p>All baptized persons, being members of the Church are subject to its discipline and entitled to the benefits thereof.</p>","text":"All baptized persons, being members of the Church are subject to its discipline and entitled to the benefits thereof."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"94a0b54eec213ad53deb08f9fe4e387f46d90e3373f4cd38647b018d7b192c88","parent_id":"bco:27","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":4,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:27-2--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Sheppard v. Highlands Presbytery","year":2023,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:27-2--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.md:occ-be44c60dd3ab","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":358},"excerpt":"[^fn-ga50-p850-n10]:BCO 27-2: “All baptized persons, being members of the Church are subject to its","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-04.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["timeliness of process","BCO 32-20 statute of limitations","strong presumption of guilt","BCO 31-2 mandatory process","judicial and pastoral procedures","case of scandal","retroactive application of BCO amendments","debarment from prosecution","stare decisis in ecclesiastical courts"],"standard_of_review":"constitutional_interpretation","review_standards":["constitutional_interpretation"],"case_numbers":["2022-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained TE Craig Sheppard's complaint against Highlands Presbytery. It held that Presbytery erred when its Judicial Commission found a strong presumption of guilt but, instead of instituting process under BCO 31-2, directed pastoral reconciliation and conditioned later process on its success; that motion also impaired the accused's right against self-incrimination. It further held that BCO 32-20's one-year time bar had run and that the 2022 amendment did not apply retroactively, so Presbytery is debarred from prosecuting the allegations. Four commissioners dissented, disputing the BCO 32-20 ruling."}},{"id":"bco:27-2--case:cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Michael Chastain v. Heritage Presbytery","year":2007,"disposition":"out_of_order","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.html","raw_u